dropped the body
--
N5008 [namespace.udecl]/3, [class.inhctor.init]/1: `using base::base;' in a
class template names the constructors of its dependent base class (here
through a member typedef, as libstdc++ writes it); they are inherited, and
`translator<T, I, C>(t)' is initialized by base's constructor.  The front
end found no constructor ("found no match for symbol 'translator'"),
dropped the constructor of the enclosing matcher and verified a wrong
result.  The dependent base was not the cause: every inherited
constructor with a single reference parameter was skipped as if it were
the base's copy or move constructor.  [over.match.funcs.general]/9
excludes only a first parameter `reference to cv P' with P related to
the base, so `translator_base(const T &)' with T = traits is inherited.  This is libstdc++'s
regex `_RegexTranslator' (`using _Base::_Base;'), used by _AnyMatcher,
_CharMatcher and _BracketMatcher (regex_compiler.h:352/373/410/434, 5
cbmc-cpp regex descs in the round-163 audit).  Header-free reduction.
Fails on the round-163 build bin52.
